    S:gt.blockmachines.largemolecularassembler.name=大型分子アセンブラー
    S:gt.blockmachines.largemolecularassembler.tooltip=Machine Type: §eMolecular Assembler, LMA§r\nNeeds a Data Orb to be placed in the controller\nUses §eCrafting Pattern Providers§r to store patterns\nBasic: §a16§7 EU/t, unaffected by overclocking\nCrafting: §a64§7 EU/t, Finish §f2§7 Jobs in §f1§7s\nThe first two Overclocks:\n-Reduce the Finish time to §f0.5§7s and §f0.25§7s\nSubsequent Overclocks:\n-Double the number of Jobs finished at once\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.largemolecularassembler.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §65§7x§65§7x§65§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front bottom center\n   §654 §fVibrant Quartz Glass\n   §624-40 §fRobust Tungstensteel Machine Casing\n   §e1+ §fEnergy Hatch: §7Any casing\n   §e1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Bus or Crafting Pattern Provider: §7Any casing\n   §fMandatory Air: §7Interior of the structure\n   \nPlace a data orb inside the controller and connect it to an AE2 network\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.lesu.name=L.E.S.U.
    S:gt.blockmachines.lesu.tooltip=Controller Block for the GT2-Styled L.E.S.U.\nSize: ANY\nStorage per LESU Casing: 20,000,000EU\nOutput EU: LESU Casings amount\nInput EU: Next Voltage Tier to Output EU\nInput/Output Amps can be configured via 4 Circuits in GUI\nOutput Side has a dot on it.\n§cOnly one Controller allowed, no Wallsharing!\nAdded by bartimaeusnek via §2BartWorks§7
    S:gt.blockmachines.lftr.controller.single.name=液体フッ化トリウム炉 [LFTR]
    S:gt.blockmachines.lftr.controller.single.tooltip=Machine Type: §eReactor§r\nController Block for the Liquid Fluoride Thorium Reactor\nProduces energy and new elements from Radioactive Beta Decay!\nInput LFTB and a molten salt as fuel, and match the four 4A dynamo hatches:\nLFTR Fuel 1 (4 EV Hatches), LFTR Fuel 2 (4 IV Hatches), LFTR Fuel 3 (4 LuV Hatches)\nIf using better hatches for a worse fuel, only 1 hatch outputs EU\nOutputs U-233 every 10 seconds, on average, while the reactor is running\nCheck NEI to see the other 3 outputs - they differ between fuels\n§54000 §7Pollution per second\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.lftr.controller.single.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §67§7x§67§7x§64§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front bottom center\n   §627-86 §fHastelloy-N Reactor Casing\n   §626 §fReactor Shield Casing\n   §e4 §fDynamo Hatch: §7Any edge casing (EV-LuV)\n   §e1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any edge casing\n   §e4 §fMuffler Hatch: §7Any top 3x3 center casing (IV+)\n   §e1+ §fInput Hatch: §7Any edge casing (IV+)\n   §e4+ §fOutput Hatch: §7Any edge casing (IV+)\n   §fMandatory Air: §7Interior of the structure\n   \n§cDynamo cannot be greater than 4A\nOne ME output hatch can replace the four regular output hatches\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.linear_accelerator.name=線形加速器
    S:gt.blockmachines.linear_accelerator.tooltip=Machine Type: §eParticle Accelerator, LINAC§r\nAccelerates particle beams to higher energies by passing them through an electric field\nElectrically neutral §5particles§7 are therefore unaffected\nUse a §bportable scanner §7for info about the input/output of this multiblock\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nRequires §fLength * 1,000 L/s§7 of §bcoolant§7 to run, returns as §chot coolant\n§bLiquid Oxygen§f: 90 K\n§bLiquid Nitrogen§f: 77 K\n§bCoolant§f: 60 K\n§bSuper Coolant§f: 1 K\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nIncreasing the length/power increases the §9Output Beam Energy§7 but decreases the §2Output Beam Focus\nPreserve §2Beam Focus§7 more effectively with lower temperature §bcoolant\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§9Output Beam Energy§f = max(§eV§f, 50) * 10^§eIE\nwhere §eV§f = 0.25 * (Length - 1) * cbrt(§3EU/t Provided§f)\nand §eIE§f = 1 + min(§9Input Beam Energy§f, 7500) / §9Max Particle Energy\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§2Output Beam Focus§f = (§2Input Beam Focus§f + §eMachine Focus§f)/2§7 if §2Input Beam Focus§f > §eMachine Focus\n§2Output Beam Focus§f = §2Input Beam Focus§f * §eMachine Focus§f/100§7 if §2Input Beam Focus§f <= §eMachine Focus\nwhere §eMachine Focus§f = min(90, max(5, (-0.9 * (Length-1) * 1.1^(0.2 * §bCoolant Temperature§f) + 110)))\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.linear_accelerator.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §619-83§7x§67§7x§67§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) \n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front bottom center\n   §6325-1285 §fShielded Accelerator Casing\n   §6148-852 §fCoolant Delivery Casing\n   §6156-732 §fElectrode Casing\n   §6127-703 §fShielded Accelerator Glass\n   §656-312 §fSuperconducting Coil Block\n   §648 §fLuV+ Tiered Glass\n   §647 §fGrate Machine Casing\n   §e1 §fBeam Input Hatch: §7Front center casing\n   §e1 §fBeam Output Hatch: §7Back center casing\n   §e1-2 §fEnergy Hatch: §7Any bottom edge casing 3-8 blocks from front\n   §e1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any bottom edge casing 3-8 blocks from front\n   §e1 §fInput Hatch: §7Top center casing 8th block from front\n   §e1 §fOutput Hatch: §7Top center casing 8th block from back\n   §fMandatory Air: §7Interior of the structure\n   \nProjector stack size determines §bLength\nSubchannel §bglass§7 determines §bGlass Tier\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
