    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.implosioncompressor.tooltip_secondary=§f寸法: §63§7x§63§7x§63§7 (§6奥行,L§7x§6幅,W§7x§6高さ,H§7) §c(中空)\n§f構造: \n   §f本体: §7正面中央、2段目\n   §616-20 §f堅牢なスチール製マシン外装\n   §e1+ §fエネルギーハッチ: §7任意の外装\n   §e1 §fメンテナンスハッチ: §7任意の外装\n   §e1 §fマフラーハッチ: §7任意の外装\n   §e1+ §f入力バス: §7任意の外装\n   §e1+ §f出力バス: §7任意の外装\n   §f空気ブロック: §7構造内部\n§7§m------------------------------\n§f構造の可視化/建設には、本体に§9 ホログラム§1プロジェクター§fを使用してください！
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.industrialfarm.name=工業用大型農場
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.industrialfarm.tooltip=機械の種類: §8《§e工業用作物栽培機§8／Industrial Crop Cultivator》§e, IF§r\n工業規模で作物を栽培\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n機械の§b奥行§7と基本電力消費量は§8《§f苗床§8／Seed Bed》§7の§cTier§7依存\n§fｱｯﾌﾟｸﾞﾚｰﾄﾞ§7の§cTier§7は§8《§f苗床§8／Seed Bed》§7の§cTier§7と一致させる\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nエネルギーハッチの電圧は§fガラス§7のTierにより制限される\n§aオーバークロック成長加速ユニット使用時、複数アンペアハッチ1台を組み込み可能！\n§a複数アンペアハッチ使用時、通常のエネルギーハッチは使用不可能\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§l[LSHIFT]§r§7 を長押しして構造体のガイドラインを表示する
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.industrialfarm.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §63-14§7x§65§7x§64§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front center, 2nd layer\n   §e1+ §fEnergy Hatch: §7Any center end casing\n   §e1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any center end casing\n   §e0+ §fInput Bus: §7Any center end casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Hatch: §7Any center end casing\n   §e1+ §fOutput Bus: §7Any center end casing\n   \n   §9Base Structure\n   §616-27 §fBricked Agricultural Casing\n   §64 §fAny Tiered Glass §b(Tiered)\n   §63 §fSeed Bed §b(Tiered)\n   §60-1 §fWood Frame Box\n   §e0-1 §fIF Upgrade Unit: §7Any wooden frame box\n   \n   §9Each Additional §bSlice\n   §64 §fAny Tiered Glass §b(Tiered)\n   §63 §fSeed Bed §b(Tiered)\n   §62 §fBricked Agricultural Casing\n   §60-1 §fWood Frame Box\n   §e0-1 §fIF Upgrade Unit: §7Any wooden frame box\n   \nProjector stack size determines §bLength\nSubchannel §bglass§7 determines §bGlass Tier\nSubchannel §bif_tier§7 determines §bControls the tier of the Industrial Farm\nSubchannel §bif_upgrade§7 determines §bEnables upgrade placement for the Industrial Farm\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.large-hadron-collider.name=大型ハドロン衝突型加速器
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.large-hadron-collider.tooltip=Machine Type: §eParticle Accelerator, Particle Collider, LHC§r\nAccelerates particles to high energies and then collides them to generate new particles\nElectrically neutral particles are unaffected\nSet the §9Target Beam Energy§7 (up to 2TeV) and the §dmaximum number of cycles§7\nCycles every second\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§f§nAccelerator mode§7\nAccelerates the beam in the smaller LHC ring\nAccelerator mode increases the §9Beam Energy§7 by §3EU Consumed in cycle§7 * §f0.1eV§7 / §6Beam Rate§7,\nuntil the §9Target Beam Energy§7 is reached, or the §dmaximum number of cycles§7 is reached\nIf the §9Target Beam Energy§7 is reached, add §f0.3§7 * §6Beam Rate§7 to the current §6Beam Rate§7\nHowever, if the current §6Beam Rate§7 >= §f5000§7, add (§f0.3§7 * §6Beam Rate§7)^§f0.5§7\nto the current §6Beam Rate§7 instead\n§3Power§7 cost starts at §f1A§7 of §fUV§7 per §6Beam Rate§7 and increases quadratically\nwith the §dnumber of completed cycles§7\n§3P§7 = (§f1A UV§7) * §6R§7 * (§dN§7+1)^2\nAutomatically switches to Collider mode when the §dmaximum number of cycles§7 is reached\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§f§nCollider mode§7\nSplits the beam into §ftwo§7 beams that go in opposite directions in the larger LHC ring, which\nthen collide to generate new particles\nThe §bCollision Energy§7 is two times the §9Beam Energy§7\nIf the §bCollision Energy§7 exceeds the rest mass of a particle, that particle will start\nappearing in the outputs\nA particle output can only appear in the modules that correspond to the forces that\ninteract with that particle\nFor example, Neutrinos cannot appear in the Strong force module, §fALICE§7, since they do\nnot interact via the strong force\n§fFiltered Beam Output Hatches§7 will allow you to see the list of possible outputs, and\nfilter them\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nThere are four LHC modules, marked by the letter on top of the module:\n§bE - Electromagnetism§7 - Charged Matter Sensor (§bCMS§7)\n§2W - Weak Interaction§7 - Advanced Total Lepton Assimilation Snare (§2ATLAS§7)\n§fS - Strong Force§7 - Absolute Lattice Integrated Chromodynamic Encapsulator (§fALICE§7)\n§5G - Gravity§7 - Localized Horizon Curvature Binder (§5LHCb§7)\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§aSupports Multi-Amp and Laser Hatches!\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines\nAdded by: §aAuthor: §6Ham§fCorp§r§7
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.large-hadron-collider.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §6122§7x§6109§7x§613§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front center of accelerator ring, 12th layer\n   §65664 §fCollider Casing\n   §673 §fNeonite (any color)\n   §620 §fShielded Accelerator Glass\n   §616 §fShielded Accelerator Casing\n   §e1 §fBeam Input Hatch: §7Entrance to accelerator ring\n   §e1+ §fEnergy Hatch: §7Any casing\n   \n   §bCMS Module §9(E)\n   §6523 §fCollider Casing\n   §6148 §fCharged Matter Sensor Casing\n   §6126 §fShielded Accelerator Glass\n   §611 §fNeonite (any color)\n   §e2 §fFiltered Beam Output Hatch: §7Inner side of module\n   \n   §bATLAS Module §9(W)\n   §6515 §fCollider Casing\n   §6160 §fAdvanced Total Lepton Assimilation Snare Casing\n   §6126 §fShielded Accelerator Glass\n   §613 §fNeonite (any color)\n   §e2 §fFiltered Beam Output Hatch: §7Inner side of module\n   \n   §bALICE Module §9(S)\n   §6517 §fCollider Casing\n   §6158 §fAbsolute Lattice Integrated Chromodynamic Encapsulator Casing\n   §6140 §fShielded Accelerator Glass\n   §611 §fNeonite (any color)\n   §e2 §fFiltered Beam Output Hatch: §7Inner side of module\n   \n   §bLHCb Module §9(G)\n   §6511 §fCollider Casing\n   §6144 §fLocalized Horizon Curvature Binder Casing\n   §6126 §fShielded Accelerator Glass\n   §617 §fNeonite (any color)\n   §e2 §fFiltered Beam Output Hatch: §7Inner side of module\n   \nProjector stack size determines §bNumber of Modules\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.large-neutralization-engine.name=Large Neutralization Engine
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.large-neutralization-engine.tooltip=Machine Type: §eAcid Generator, LNE§r\n(Dis)solves all your problems!\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nCan §fuse §7a §bbase §7to boost §defficiency §7(consumes one by one):\n§bSodium Hydroxide§7 : §d150%§7 : §f60§7/§fminute\n§bPotassium Hydroxide§7 : §d190%§7 : §f24§7/§fminute\n§bCaesium Hydroxide§7 : §d250%§7 : §f6§7/§fminute\n§bFrancium Hydroxide§7 : §d500%§7 : §f5§7/§fminute\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nProduces §cToxic Residue §7from burning acids\nIf the §cToxic Residue §7exceeds the §3Capacity§7, the multiblock will §4EXPLODE!\nEvery §ftick§7, §cToxic Residue §7will §fincrease §7by §6Residue Rate§7*§eFuel Consumption(L)§7*rand(§f0.7§7,§f1.3§7)\n§6Residue Rate §7is calculated as §f0.05§7*§dBase Fuel Value (EU/L)§7^§f0.8\nEvery §ftick§7, §cToxic Residue §7will §fdecrease §7by §9Base Decay§7*§eDecay Boost§7*(§cToxic Residue§7^§f0.08§7)\nResidue will decay §f10 §7times slower when multiblock is disabled\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nInsert §dRobot Arms §7to increase §eDecay Boost§7:\n§eDecay Boost §7is calculated as §f1.2§7^§dRobot Arm Tier §7if §aIV §7or below, §f1.4§7^§dRobot Arm Tier §7if §dLuV §7or above\nInsert §dmultiple §7(§f16 §7max) robot arms to multiply §eDecay Boost §7by sqrt(§dRobot Arm Amount§7)\nEvery §fminute§7, §dRobot Arm Amount§7/(§f45§7*(§f1§7+§dRobot Arm Tier§7)) chance for §fone §7used robot arm to §cvoid\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nStructure has §f3 Tiers§7, §fTier §7determines §9Base Decay §7and §3Capacity§7:\n§fT1§7 : §fStrengthened Inanimate Machine Casing§7 : §9200§7 : §3375,000\n§fT2§7 : §fPrecise Stationary Machine Casing§7 : §9400§7 : §31,000,000\n§fT3§7 : §fUltimate Static Machine Casing§7 : §9700§7 : §32,500,000\n§aSupports Multi-Amp and Laser Hatches!\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.large-neutralization-engine.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §63§7x§611§7x§67§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Hollow)\n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Top center, 6th layer\n   §630-43 §fMachine Casing §b(Tiered)\n   §634 §fPTFE Frame Box\n   §615 §fPTFE Pipe Casing\n   §e0+ §fToxic Residue Sensor Hatch: §7Any machine casing\n   §e1+ §fDynamo Hatch: §7Any machine casing\n   §e1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any machine casing\n   §e0+ §fInput Bus: §7Any machine casing\n   §e1+ §fInput Hatch: §7Any machine casing\n   \nProjector stack size determines §bCasing Tier\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
