    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.oredrill4.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §63§7x§63§7x§67§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) \n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front bottom center\n   §615 §fOsmiridium Frame Box\n   §65-7 §fMining Osmiridium Casing\n   §e1-2 §fEnergy Hatch: §7Any bottom casing (IV+)\n   §e1 §fMaintenance Hatch: §7Any bottom casing\n   §e0-1 §fInput Bus: §7Any bottom casing\n   §e1 §fInput Hatch: §7Any bottom casing\n   §e1 §fOutput Bus: §7Any bottom casing\n   \n§cDon't forget to protect the machine from rain and/or meteors!\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.oreprocessor.name=統合鉱石ファクトリー
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.oreprocessor.tooltip=Machine Type: §eOre Processor, IOF§r\n§4DEPRECATED - Controller will be removed in next major update!\n§4Check NEI for new Controller and conversion recipe\nDoes all ore processing in one step\n§61024§7 Parallels\nEvery ore costs 30EU/t, 2L lubricant, 200L distilled water\nRecipes that need extra input require their extra inputs on top of the normal costs\nProcessing time is dependent on mode\nUse a screwdriver to switch mode\nSneak click with screwdriver to void the stone dust\n§5200 §7Pollution per second\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§aOP stands for Ore Processor ;)\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.multimachine.oreprocessor.tooltip.15564=Machine Type: §eOre Processor, IOF§r\nDoes all ore processing in one step\nParallel count scales with total input power: EU/t / 30\nEvery ore costs 30EU/t, 2L lubricant, 200L distilled water\nRecipes that need extra input require their extra inputs on top of the normal costs\nProcessing time is dependent on mode\nUse a screwdriver to switch mode\nSneak click with screwdriver to void the stone dust\n§aSupports Multi-Amp and Laser Hatches!\n§5200 §7Pollution per second\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§aOP stands for Ore Processor ;)\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines\nStructure by: §a§6Bavib§r§7
