    S:gt.blockmachines.yottafluidtank.name=YOTタンク
    S:gt.blockmachines.yottafluidtank.tooltip=Machine Type: §eFluid Tank§r\nThe max output speed is decided by the amount of stored liquid and the output hatch's capacity\nThe max fluid cell tier is limited by the glass tier\nHV glass for T1, EV glass for T2, IV glass for T3. . .\nThe max height of the cell blocks is 15\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidelines
    S:gt.blockmachines.yottafluidtank.tooltip_secondary=§fDimensions: §65§7x§65§7x§65-19§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) \n§fStructure: \n   §fController: §7Front center, 2nd layer\n   §e0-1 §fYOTHatch: §7Any bottom center casing (replaces other hatches)\n   §e1+ §fInput Hatch: §7Any top center casing\n   §e1+ §fOutput Hatch: §7Any bottom center casing\n   \n   §9Base Structure\n   §625-57 §fYOTTank Casing\n   §616 §fSteel Frame Box\n   §616 §fAny Tiered Glass §b(Tiered)\n   §69 §fFluid Cell Block §b(Tiered)\n   \n   §9Each Additional §bLayer\n   §616 §fAny Tiered Glass §b(Tiered)\n   §69 §fFluid Cell Block §b(Tiered)\n   \nNo air gaps allowed, but the fluid cell blocks can be different tiers\nProjector stack size determines §bHeight\nSubchannel §bglass§7 determines §bGlass Tier\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f to visualize/build the structure!
    S:gt.blockmachines.yottafluidtankhatch.name=YOTハッチ
    S:gt.blockmachines.yottafluidtankhatch.tooltip=Special I/O port for AE2FC.\nDirectly connected YOTTank with AE fluid storage system.\nUse screwdriver to set storage priority\nUse soldering iron to set read/write mode\nUse wire cutter to enable/disable sticky mode
